{"id": "EUVD-2026-108797", "enisaUuid": "f095f46d-a9aa-33cf-8132-533ba505e0a4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/panthor: validate userspace queue count against initialized firmware slot count\n\nIn panthor_drv.c:panthor_ioctl_group_create(),\nthe queue count is validated against the hardcoded maximum:\n\n\tif (!args->queues.count || args->queues.count > MAX_CS_PER_CSG)\n\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n\nHowever, if the firmware reports fewer slots than MAX_CS_PER_CSG,\npanthor_fw_init_ifaces() will only initialize that smaller number of\nstream interfaces.\n\nIf unprivileged userspace requests more queues than the firmware reported\n(but no more than MAX_CS_PER_CSG), cs_slot_prog_locked() fetches an\nuninitialized stream interface and may crash when dereferencing\ncs_iface->input->ringbuf_base.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:20:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:20:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4487cf79bf173f2b426a02d102076f8a20d23b96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fdee3570b282a6c8699aea63fa5694355e010ec9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9be126be5f78bc331a930295af97c9b1f9158f06", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ec86c43dcfff68eab4db9bdafcd3e2b16e342e18"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99003"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2811b284-6a57-369c-bef8-109a4adb1991", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de85488138247d034eb3241840424a54d660926b <4487cf79bf173f2b426a02d102076f8a20d23b96"}, {"id": "2e87e914-d72b-3100-8be0-16751055f391", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "32a0e13b-ec58-3a79-a3ed-671c20667387", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de85488138247d034eb3241840424a54d660926b <ec86c43dcfff68eab4db9bdafcd3e2b16e342e18"}, {"id": "4bc7345e-db90-3ec9-b42b-dffb314d6145", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "58ce2a42-9df1-32a3-abf5-5a0a10edfd55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de85488138247d034eb3241840424a54d660926b <fdee3570b282a6c8699aea63fa5694355e010ec9"}, {"id": "761492e2-e1ce-3605-97dd-56529ec0a810", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "830acf3c-4221-35d6-a36b-6b203c877925", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "859cb104-8a7d-33c4-bda1-d3633725616e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de85488138247d034eb3241840424a54d660926b <9be126be5f78bc331a930295af97c9b1f9158f06"}, {"id": "dab51e1a-894a-3579-80ba-f53659245d2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "f87f9b82-7326-3857-89b4-6fa7407681dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "81374ca3-d3ef-3d50-a9f2-06d250f7bc4e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}